{
  "uid": "boomtime-reading-monitor",
  "title": "boomtime · Reading monitor (whispersync cadence)",
  "description": "The empirical probe for the Kindle two-level polling model (see catalyst-books-domain-architecture.md §5.1). Kindle reading time is reconstructed by polling — Amazon never pushes — so this board derives the recommended poll intervals from your own reading: p50 advance interval ≈ the fine capture interval T2, p90 ≈ the idle gap G. First-party Prometheus metrics (mimir) up top, the per-book advance log (Loki loki-v2) at the bottom.",
  "tags": [
    "apps",
    "boomtime",
    "domain",
    "books",
    "kindle",
    "reading-monitor"
  ],
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "1m",
  "timezone": "browser",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "source",
        "type": "query",
        "label": "Source",
        "description": "The reading source label carried on every reading-monitor metric (bounded — no per-title cardinality). Default All is the regex .+, so a new source appears without editing the board.",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "mimir"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(boomtime_reading_monitor_advances_total, source)",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(boomtime_reading_monitor_advances_total, source)",
        "regex": "",
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".+",
        "multi": true,
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "hide": 0,
        "skipUrlSync": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Whispersync cadence — the two-level polling model",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Kindle reading time is **reconstructed by polling** — Amazon never pushes, and the sidecar is per-book. So the engine runs two levels: **L1 (detect)** polls every in-progress book at a coarse interval **`T1`** to spot which book advanced; **L2 (capture)** then polls only the active book(s) at a fine interval **`T2`** until idle for a gap **`G`**, then drops back to L1. This collapses cost from *every book fast, always* to *every book slow + the 1–2 actually being read fast*.\n\nThis board is the **empirical probe** for picking `T1`/`T2`/`G` from **your own** reading instead of a guessed `interval=6s`:\n\n- **p50 advance interval ≈ `T2`** — the whispersync push cadence; no point sampling faster than Amazon writes the LPR.\n- **p90 advance interval ≈ `G`** — the longest gap *within* a real session; the idle threshold before dropping back to L1.\n- **active books / advance rate** — how much fine-capture work is live right now.\n\nMetrics come from the **persistent leader-singleton monitor** (runs whether or not the admin panel is open). Detail: `docs/design/catalyst-books-domain-architecture.md` §5.1."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Active books",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(boomtime_reading_monitor_active_books{namespace=\"boomtime\", source=~\"$source\"})",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "mimir"
          },
          "legendFormat": "active"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "value": null,
                "color": "blue"
              },
              {
                "value": 1,
                "color": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "values": false,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "description": "Books currently in L2 fine-capture (actively being read right now) across the selected source(s)."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Advance rate",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(boomtime_reading_monitor_advances_total{namespace=\"boomtime\", source=~\"$source\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "mimir"
          },
          "legendFormat": "adv/s"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "values": false,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "description": "Whispersync location advances detected per second."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "p50 advance interval (≈ T2)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum(rate(boomtime_reading_monitor_advance_interval_seconds_bucket{namespace=\"boomtime\", source=~\"$source\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (le))",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "mimir"
          },
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "green"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "values": false,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "description": "Median gap between consecutive whispersync advances — the observed push cadence. This is the recommended fine capture interval T2 (sampling faster buys nothing)."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "p90 advance interval (≈ G)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.90, sum(rate(boomtime_reading_monitor_advance_interval_seconds_bucket{namespace=\"boomtime\", source=~\"$source\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (le))",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "mimir"
          },
          "legendFormat": "p90"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "yellow"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "values": false,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "description": "90th-percentile advance gap — a proxy for the longest gap still inside one reading session. This is the recommended idle threshold G before L2 drops back to coarse L1 polling."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "p99 advance interval",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 20,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(boomtime_reading_monitor_advance_interval_seconds_bucket{namespace=\"boomtime\", source=~\"$source\"}[$__rate_interval])) by (le))",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "mimir"
          },
          "legendFormat": "p99"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "orange"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "values": false,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "description": "Tail advance gap. Well above p90 means either genuine session boundaries or L1 detection latency (a session started while polling coarse) — the T1 tradeoff."
    },
